    "scope": "TOML 1.0.0 text from a local file into a Jackson JsonNode tree; with PARSE_JAVA_TIME the four date/time kinds are java.time values in POJONodes",
    "family": "Jackson TOML (own JFlex Lexer and recursive Parser in com.fasterxml.jackson.dataformat.toml)",
    "family_note": "jackson-dataformat-toml tokenizes and parses TOML with its own JFlex-generated Lexer and hand-written Parser; it does not use the jackson-core JSON tokenizer. It builds the result with jackson-databind's JsonNodeFactory, so jackson-core/jackson-databind 2.23.0 are shared with the Java JSON cell's jackson-core and jackson-databind paths (same Jackson project family, different format parser). Coverage and AFL++ feedback are scoped to the com.fasterxml.jackson.dataformat.toml package.",
    "configuration_note": "TomlReadFeature.PARSE_JAVA_TIME (documented, default off) is enabled. With the default, offset date-times, local date-times, local dates and local times are returned as TextNodes holding the source text, indistinguishable from strings, and offset date-times are not normalized. Floats are returned as DecimalNode (BigDecimal); the harness converts with doubleValue() because TOML floats are IEEE 754 binary64, then prints the shortest round-trip digits positionally.",
    "control": "controls/toml/service-config.toml",
